{%- comment -%}
  fye-founder — editorial two-column story with a real blockquote. 2 uses on
  page.about-us: "Why we started" (photo left, quotation) and "Meet Edward"
  (photo right, sign-off line).

  PORTED FROM LIVE'S `fye-founder`, 25/08/2026 About Us handoff. Every setting
  ID is kept, so the live template's settings carry over unchanged:
    band · image_right · image · image_position · image_alt · caption ·
    placeholder · eyebrow · heading · intro · quote · attr_name · attr_role ·
    outro · sig

  CHANGED FOR v3: the `.fye-edu` wrapper div is gone (v3 has no education
  shell — the band IS the section), colours come from tokens rather than the
  edu-core variables (`--muted` -> `--ink-soft`, `--font-head` ->
  `--font-display`), and spacing is on the --s scale.

  WHY THIS EXISTS RATHER THAN fye-media-text: media-text can do image + prose,
  but not a <figure><blockquote>…<figcaption> pair. The quotation has to be a
  real blockquote with attribution, and it has to stay visually restrained —
  the brief explicitly ruled out an oversized decorative pull-quote, which is
  what a media-text body would have needed to become.

  CLASS NAMESPACE IS `fdr`, NOT `fnd` (18/09/2026). It was `fnd`, which
  sections/fye-finder-entry.liquid also uses. Every section stylesheet block
  lands in the same styles.css bundle, concatenated by filename, so this file's
  `.fye .fnd { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 42fr 58fr }` was applied to
  the matchmaker entry band on every page it appears on - fye-founder sorts
  after fye-finder-entry, so it won even though the two sections never share a
  page. The matchmaker's .wrap became the 42fr track: an 806px box jammed
  against the left edge with an empty column beside it, which is exactly the
  symptom the 10/09 "the section owns its own width" comment in
  fye-finder-entry.liquid was trying to cure. `.fnd__name` collided too. Do not
  rename this back, and keep new class namespaces unique across ALL sections.

  The quote and the sig are alternatives, not partners: quote for someone
  else's words about us, sig for first-person copy in Ed's voice. Setting both
  reads as a man quoting himself.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign band = s.band | default: 'white'
  assign focal = s.image_position | default: 'center center'
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  Built here, not inline in image_tag. Filters cannot be chained inside a
  filter argument: passing "style: s.image_position | append" applies append to
  image_tag's OUTPUT, which printed "object-position:" and ";" as text around
  the photograph on 02/09/2026.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture img_style -%}object-position: {{ focal }};{%- endcapture -%}

<section class="fdr-sect band band--{{ band }}" data-screen-label="About — {{ s.heading | default: 'story' }}">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="fdr{% if s.image_right %} fdr--rev{% endif %}">

      <div class="fdr__media">
        {%- if s.image != blank -%}
          {{ s.image | image_url: width: 1000 | image_tag:
             loading: 'lazy',
             widths: '440, 700, 1000',
             sizes: '(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 42vw',
             class: 'fdr__img',
             alt: s.image_alt,
             style: img_style }}
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="fdr__ph" role="presentation">
            <span>{{ s.placeholder | default: 'Photograph to be added' }}</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.caption != blank -%}
          <p class="fdr__cap">{{ s.caption }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="fdr__body">
        {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="fdr__h">{{ s.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.intro != blank -%}
          <div class="prose fdr__prose">{{ s.intro }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.quote != blank -%}
          <figure class="fdr__quote">
            <blockquote>{{ s.quote }}</blockquote>
            {%- if s.attr_name != blank or s.attr_role != blank -%}
              <figcaption>
                {%- if s.attr_name != blank -%}<span class="fdr__name">{{ s.attr_name }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                {%- if s.attr_role != blank -%}<span class="fdr__role">{{ s.attr_role }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              </figcaption>
            {%- endif -%}
          </figure>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.outro != blank -%}
          <div class="prose fdr__prose">{{ s.outro }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.sig != blank -%}
          <p class="fdr__sig">{{ s.sig }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.fye .fdr {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 42fr 58fr;
  gap: var(--s10);
  align-items: start;
}
/* Order, not direction: `direction: rtl` would flip the prose too. */
.fye .fdr--rev .fdr__media { order: 2; }

.fye .fdr__body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--s5); }
.fye .fdr__h { margin: 0; }

.fye .fdr__img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
.fye .fdr__ph {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;
  justify-content: flex-end;
  aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
  padding: var(--s5);
  background: var(--ivory);
  border: var(--hairline);
}
.fye .fdr__ph span {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}
.fye .fdr__cap { margin: var(--s2) 0 0; font-size: var(--fs-fine); color: var(--ink-soft); }

/* ~62-68 characters is the reading measure this page is set to. */
.fye .fdr__prose { max-width: 36em; }
.fye .fdr__prose :where(p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }

/* Marked out by a rule and a tint, not by giant display type. */
.fye .fdr__quote {
  margin: 0;
  padding: var(--s5) var(--s6);
  max-width: 36em;
  background: var(--white);
  border-left: 2px solid var(--teal);
}
/* On white the tint has to invert or the quote disappears into the band. */
.fye .band--white .fdr__quote { background: var(--ivory); }
.fye .fdr__quote blockquote {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  quotes: none;
  font-size: var(--fs-body);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  font-style: normal;
  line-height: 1.65;
}
.fye .fdr__quote blockquote::before,
.fye .fdr__quote blockquote::after { content: none; }
.fye .fdr__quote blockquote :where(p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }
.fye .fdr__quote figcaption { margin-top: var(--s4); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
.fye .fdr__name {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-h2);
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.fye .fdr__role {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}
.fye .fdr__sig {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .fye .fdr { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s7); }
  .fye .fdr--rev .fdr__media { order: 0; }
  /* 4:5 stacked is a very tall photograph on a phone. */
  .fye .fdr__img,
  .fye .fdr__ph { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
  .fye .fdr__prose,
  .fye .fdr__quote { max-width: none; }
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .fdr__quote { padding: var(--s4) var(--s4); }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Founder story",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "band", "label": "Background", "default": "white",
      "options": [
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
        { "value": "ivory", "label": "Champagne ivory" },
        { "value": "mist",  "label": "Mist blue" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "image_right", "label": "Photograph on the right", "default": false },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Photograph" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph" },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "image_position", "label": "Focal point", "default": "center center",
      "info": "Which part to keep when cropped — e.g. center center, center 30%, top center."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Photograph description" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "caption", "label": "Caption below the photograph" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "placeholder", "label": "Placeholder caption", "default": "Photograph to be added" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Story" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading" },
    { "type": "html", "id": "intro", "label": "Opening paragraphs" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Quotation" },
    {
      "type": "html", "id": "quote", "label": "Quotation",
      "info": "Rendered as a real blockquote. Use this OR the sign-off line below, not both."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "attr_name", "label": "Attribution name" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "attr_role", "label": "Attribution role" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Closing" },
    { "type": "html", "id": "outro", "label": "Closing paragraphs" },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "sig", "label": "Sign-off line",
      "info": "For first-person copy, e.g. \"Edward — Founder, For Your Eternity\"."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Founder story" }]
}
{% endschema %}
